  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "On the island of Rodrigues the European couple and set dances - the kotis (schottische), polka, waltz, mazok (mazurka), quadrille and the local laval - survive as a living repertoire played on the diatonic button accordion, which the island's music is almost entirely built on, over drum and triangle; it is kept distinct from the island's sega tambour. The general accordion card stands in for the two-row button accordion.",
